Sword Strike (N64brew Game Jam 2024, code/swordstrike at 0dea720) for the Fire TV remote.

The game moves on the D-pad, jumps on A, attacks on B, drops through a platform on Down + A and
slides on L. A remote is held in one hand and its D-pad and OK sit under one thumb, so two buttons
at once are out, and it has no L or Z. With this patch and N64_REMOTE_MAP_DEFAULT="ok=B"
(apps/n64-swordstrike/CMakeLists.txt):
  - Left / Right move, Up jumps (as well as A), OK attacks (B);
  - Down alone drops through a platform (Down + A still does);
  - C-left / C-right, the remote's << and >>, slide left / right (L still slides the way you face);
  - the pause screen quits on B held for half a second (hold OK), as well as on Z + Up;
  - the remote's controls show below the lowest floor during the countdown and the fight's first
    5 seconds, and minigame_def.instructions lists both sets.

A gamepad keeps every original control. n64/jam24/Makefile applies this to a copy of
code/swordstrike in the build directory, so the jam checkout stays as fetched. The build stops if it
no longer applies.

